---
import CopyCommand from "./copy-command.astro";

const gitignore = `.storybranch/actual/
.storybranch/diff/
.storybranch/report.json`;

const agents = `## storybranch

Storybook 10+ must already be running. Until storybranch is on npm, invoke \`bun /path/to/storybranch/apps/cli/src/cli.ts\`. After publish, \`bunx storybranch\` is the same CLI.

- \`test --url <storybook>\` — exit 1 means a visual diff. Lines: \`missing baseline\`, \`pixels\`, \`size\`, \`stale\`. A clean run prints \`ok\`.
- Read \`.storybranch/report.json\` (\`new\`, \`changed\`, \`unchanged\`, \`stale\`, \`error\`).
- The first run is \`missing baseline\` for every shot.
- Commit only \`.storybranch/baseline/\`. Ignore \`actual/\`, \`diff/\`, and \`report.json\`.
- Run \`approve\` only when asked to accept the shots. \`review\` and \`--open\` are for a person.`;
---

<section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20" id="agents">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
      For agents in your app
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink-muted sm:text-lg">
      Paste the ignore rules into the app that owns the baselines, and the note into that repo’s AGENTS.md.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">.gitignore</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Keep{" "}
        <code class="font-mono break-all text-ink">.storybranch/baseline/</code> tracked.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <CopyCommand command={gitignore} prompt={false} />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">AGENTS.md</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Exit 1 on the first run is the baseline set. Approve only when a person asked for it.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <CopyCommand command={agents} prompt={false} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
